PCT-SCAN-ROS2 is a multi-license source distribution.

There is no single license that replaces the licenses of every included
component.  Each ROS package and vendored source subtree retains its upstream
license:

* SCAN planner and most simulator packages: Apache License 2.0
* Vendored PCT planner, tomography, and pct_scan_bridge: GPL-2.0-or-later
* local_sensing_node and mockamap: GPL-3.0-only, as declared by those packages
* Go2 description and utility packages: BSD-3-Clause, as declared by those
  packages

The complete Apache-2.0, GPL-2.0 and GPL-3.0 license texts are in LICENSES/.
Copyright notices, upstream links, and modification notes are in NOTICE,
src/pct/NOTICE, and the source files themselves.

Scene data and generated assets are licensed separately from the software.
See each assets/<scene>/README.md before redistributing them.  In particular,
the Spiral source repository does not currently state an explicit license, so
the Spiral PCD and derived tomogram are deliberately excluded from Git and are
downloaded/generated locally.

SPDX package expressions are recorded in each package.xml.  This file is a
license map, not legal advice and not an attempt to relicense upstream work.
